We need to evaluate each claim against evidence. Provide verdicts list with id, supported true/false, reason short.

We have claims C1-C8, X1-X3. Let's check each.

C1: claim about subject details. Evidence includes tool summary profile_account and Q-8709a801e8 customer record. Both show institution A, name Leon & Doyle Partners, Partnership, CN, Precious metals, risk Low, PEP false, declared monthly turnover $4,800,000. So supported.

C2: claim about inbound/outbound counts and totals. Evidence Q-b9c264f106 activity summary shows exactly those numbers. Supported.

C3: claim about largest outbound counterparty 3:80302E360 (Institution A, Partnership, CN, Restaurants) with 14 transactions worth $1,693,097. Evidence tool summary get_counterparties says largest: 3:80302E360 (A, Partnership, CN) 14 tx, $1,693,097. Q-2874bbb224 shows row with cp_bank 3, cp_account 80302E360, n_tx 14, usd_total 1693097.41, institution A, customer_type Partnership, country CN, occupation_or_industry Restaurants, risk Low. Claim matches. Supported.

C4: claim only inbound counterparty is 14:801AACAA0 (Institution B, Corporation, CN, Healthcare clinic) with a single cheque of $1,555,354. Evidence tool summary get_counterparties says 1 counterparty at Institution B, largest 14:801AACAA0 (B, Corporation, CN) 1 tx $1,555,354. Q-16e5f22ea2 shows row with those details, top_format Cheque. Supported.

C5: claim two-hop follow-the-money outbound shows 42 transactions to 16 accounts (7 A / 9 B) then 75 transactions to 12 accounts (6 A / 6 B) totalling $6.21M; 78 cross-institution transactions; no returns to origin and no convergence. Evidence follow_money summary: hop1 42 tx, 16 accounts (7 A,9 B) about $1,793,543; hop2 75 tx, 12 accounts (6 A,6 B) about $6,214,537; 78 cross-institution. analyze_network signals: cycle context 0/3 (no returns), convergence context 0/3 (no convergence). Claim matches. Supported.

C6: claim two-hop follow-the-money inbound shows 1 transaction from 1 B account then 6 transactions from 2 A accounts totalling $13,922; 7 cross-institution transactions; no returns and no convergence. Evidence follow_money summary: hop1 1 tx, 1 account (1 at B) about $1,555,354; hop2 6 tx, 2 accounts (2 at A) about $13,922; 7 cross-institution. analyze_network cycle 0, convergence 0. Claim matches. Supported.

C7: inference about network signals: burst suspicious (7 distinct counterparties in busiest 24h vs 1.7 avg, 4.0x). All structural signals (cycle, layered_transfers, convergence, interconnection, pass_through, uniform_amounts, hubs) are assessed as context with strength 0. Evidence analyze_network lists signals: burst suspicious 1/3, cycle context 0/3, one_off_transfers context 0/3, layered_transfers context 0/3, convergence context 0/3, interconnection context 0/3, pass_through context 0/3, uniform_amounts context 0/3, turnover_vs_declared context 0/3, cross_institution context 0/3, hubs context 0/3, channels context 0/3, counterparty_mix context 0/3. The claim lists structural signals: cycle, layered_transfers, convergence, interconnection, pass_through, uniform_amounts, hubs. All are context 0/3. So supported.

C8: claim watchlist screening found no match for subject; 16 Institution B counterparties could not be screened because B withholds names and DOB. Evidence screen_watchlist summary: Screened 16 Institution A customers against 1510 watchlist entries. No watchlist match for subject 3:801AAC500. 16 Institution B counterparties not screenable: names withheld by B. Matches. Supported.

X1: claim no cycle detected – no ring of similar-sized payments returns to subject. Evidence analyze_network cycle context 0/3 says exactly that. Also Q-df7cada130 shows 0 rows. Supported.

X2: claim no layered transfers – none of subject’s outbound payments were passed on (or funded) by another transfer within 72h. Evidence analyze_network layered_transfers context 0/3 says exactly that. Supported.

X3: claim no convergence – no non-hub account collects from or funds several of subject’s counterparties. Evidence analyze_network convergence context 0/3 says exactly that. Supported.

All claims supported true.

